15 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic showing univariate \(A\) and multivariable AIC \(B\) analyses of clinical variables with hazard ratios, confidence intervals, and p values for each variable related to patient outcomes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Nomogram diagram displaying predictors and point scales for ECOG, TP, ALP, SII, and PLR metrics, allowing total points calculation and conversion to linear predictor, one-year overall survival, and two-year overall survival probabilities.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Three-panel figure displaying survival model performance assessment in training, internal validation, and external validation cohorts. Panel A shows time-dependent ROC curves comparing one-year and two-year AUC values for each cohort. Panel B presents calibration curves, with observed versus predicted survival probabilities at one and two years in each cohort, including error bars. Panel C contains decision curve analysis \(DCA\) plots for one-year and two-year survival, visualizing standardized net benefit versus high-risk threshold or cost-benefit ratio.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Three Kaplan\205Meier plots compare overall survival between the low- and high-risk groups in the training, internal validation, and external validation cohorts. In all three cohorts, the low-risk group shows higher overall survival than the high-risk group. Risk tables below each plot show the numbers of patients at risk over time. The differences between the risk groups are statistically significant in the training cohort \(P  < 0.0001\), internal validation cohort \(P  < 0.0001\), and external validation cohort \(P = 0.0044\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Two Kaplan\205Meier survival curves display overall survival probability over time for low risk \(left\) and high risk \(right\) groups, comparing ICI alone \(red\) and ICI plus TRT \(blue\). The low risk group shows significantly improved survival with ICI plus TRT \(p = 0.00079\), with median survival time not reached, compared to 40.5 months for ICI alone. In the high risk group, survival does not differ significantly between treatments \(p = 0.72\), with median survival times of 16.3 months for ICI and 19.8 months for ICI plus TRT. Tables beneath each plot list number at risk at various time points.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Two Kaplan-Meier survival curves compare overall survival in low-risk and high-risk groups after propensity score matching, analyzing ICI \(red\) versus ICI plus TRT \(blue\) treatments over time. For the low-risk group, ICI+TRT shows higher survival probability with a statistically significant difference \(p = 0.036, HR = 0.532, 95% CI: 0.292-0.97\). For the high-risk group, there is no significant difference \(p = 0.89, HR = 1.047, 95% CI: 0.519-2.11\). Tables below each graph display the number at risk for each group at different time intervals.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Four Kaplan\205Meier survival plots are arranged in two panels. Panel A shows overall survival in the low-risk group, stratified by treatment response \(CR/PR and SD/PD\), comparing ICI alone with ICI plus TRT. Panel B shows the corresponding comparisons in the high-risk group. P values, median survival times, and numbers at risk at different time points are displayed. ICI is shown in red and ICI plus TRT in blue.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Two Kaplan\205Meier plots compare overall survival according to TRT pattern in the low- and high-risk groups. Patients are classified as receiving no TRT, consolidative TRT, or salvage TRT. In the low-risk group, overall survival differs significantly among the three groups \(P = 0.0034\), with the consolidative and salvage TRT curves showing higher observed survival than the no-TRT group. In the high-risk group, no statistically significant difference is observed among the three groups \(P = 0.90\). Median survival times and numbers at risk are displayed.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Two Kaplan\205Meier plots compare overall survival according to BED10 category in the low- and high-risk groups. Patients are classified as receiving no TRT, BED10  <60 Gy, or BED10  >60 Gy. In the low-risk group, overall survival differs significantly among the three groups \(P = 0.001\), with the BED10 >60 Gy group showing the highest observed survival and a median survival time that was not reached. In the high-risk group, survival is similar among the three groups, with no statistically significant difference \(P = 0.824\). Median survival times and numbers at risk are displayed.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Forest plot comparing hazard ratios for death between ICI+TRT and ICI alone across oligometastatic and polymetastatic subgroups within low-risk and high-risk groups. Low-risk, polymetastatic group shows significantly lower hazard ratio with ICI+TRT \(HR 0.399, confidence interval 0.213 to 0.747, P 0.004\). Other subgroups show no statistically significant differences. Hazard ratios and confidence intervals are visually represented with black dots and horizontal lines; results also presented in a table alongside P-interaction values for each group.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
